<title>GERMANY: German trade seeks free market barley export.</title>
<headline>German trade seeks free market barley export.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders bid for the export of 8,000 tonnes of free market barley with rebates in a 19.95-28.40 Ecus a tonne range, the state grain intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bids will be considered at the European Union's weekly cereals management committee meeting later today.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
